---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { homeSchema } from '../data/demos';
import Opener from '../components/sections/Opener.astro';
import Door from '../components/sections/Door.astro';
import Cta from '../components/sections/Cta.astro';
import { doors, heroTool } from '../data/home';
import { industrialPrice } from '../data/services';

const origin = new URL(Astro.site!).origin;
---
<MarketingLayout
  title="AppliedIQ Solutions"
  description="Supply chain planning tools built to order for one plant on its own extract, by someone who works a planning floor. Open every one first, on invented data. Local websites and tools are on Main Street."
  schema={homeSchema(origin)}
>
  {/* THE PITCH, not a navigation hub (D29), AND SINCE D118 THE PITCH IS THREE
      DOORS. The operator's words on 2026-09-20: "streamline my site and
      eliminate all of the overwhelming noise", focusing on websites, local
      small business and industrial tools. Seven bands became four: the opener,
      then one door per offer, then the closing call. Nothing opens on this page
      itself; the shelf, the free check and the founding offer are one click
      away on Main Street, under the local door.

      ── THE SHAPE IS HIS PICK, 2026-09-20 ─────────────────────────────────────

      He chose arrangement 1 of a three-way shape pack — "doors stacked; Main
      Street opens on the founding offer" — over a one-row trio (which reads as
      a menu, the thing the last home page was cut for) and a local door
      carrying the whole shelf (which grows with it, the length the last home
      page was also cut for). Sign-off: ~/.claude/.shape-signed/. His rider, in
      his words: "I don't want to lose the elegance and the twin river theme of
      my existing site design/theme." So the oyster ground, the crape-myrtle
      accent, Fraunces, the restraint and the two-currents backdrop are exactly
      what they were. Arrangement changed; theme did not.

      ── THE GROUNDS ARE THE ARGUMENT, not decoration (D113's rule) ────────────

      SINCE 2026-09-27 (D125) the order below is the one that renders; the
      websites door and its surface ground left with the move to planning first.

        Opener        canvas · widest column · display XL · loose
        Manufacturers INSTRUMENT · feature · the floor per plant · the phone-only shot
        Main Street   DEEP · popout · tight · the 3px rule
        Cta           canvas · centered · narrow

      Every neighbor pair differs on at least two of ground, column and density,
      which is the fix src/components/kit/industrial.js records under WHY THREE
      AND NOT SEVEN: a hue is the lightest signal on a page, so the doors are
      told apart by ground lightness, column and rhythm rather than by color.

      THE LOCAL DOOR'S PORTAL TILE LEFT THE OPENER. It was the geographic door
      while the home page had no local band; a tile and a full band saying the
      same sentence on one screen is the redundancy D102 cuts.

      WHAT LEFT WITH D118: the tools band (now on Main Street), the free-check
      ledger (Main Street), the objection (on /websites/ since Phase 3), the
      assessment band (Main Street), the proof-at-scale grid and the doorway it
      carried. Breadth.astro stays for /bio/.

      NO SECTION COUNT IS WRITTEN HERE. `node scripts/print-home-order.mjs`
      prints what the built page actually paints, heading by heading.

      Copy lives in src/data/home.ts; the figure comes from services.ts. */}
  <Opener />

  {/* PLANNING LEADS, SINCE 2026-09-27 (D125). The manufacturers door comes
      first, carrying the floor per plant and its qualifier in one box, and the
      phone-only screenshot the Opener shows on desktop, so it renders once at
      every width. The websites door left this page: a website is an offer for a
      local or small business now, reached through Main Street, and
      verify-website.mjs checks this page paints neither its figure nor a link
      to it. */}
  <Door
    {...doors.manufacturers}
    tone="instrument"
    width="feature"
    density="regular"
    panel={{ line: industrialPrice.line, qualifier: industrialPrice.qualifier }}
    shot={{ src: heroTool.shot, alt: heroTool.shotAlt, href: heroTool.cta.href }}
  />

  <Door
    {...doors.local}
    tone="deep"
    width="popout"
    density="tight"
  />

  <Cta />
</MarketingLayout>
